    "q-96570": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96570",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=5)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "We construct an interval around $X=5$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14129188/assets/b87c1f5bb39d9bd7fe5a46695eb8428909fc40c0e489fd12b054bbd77be8127f.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & ≈P(5-0.5\\le Y\\le 5+0.5) \\\\  & =P(4.5\\le Y\\le 5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
