    "q-96134": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96134",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(1<X<5)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<5) & =P(2\\le X\\le 4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $2\\le X\\le 4$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 4) & ≈P(2-0.5\\le Y\\le 4+0.5) \\\\  & =P(1.5\\le Y\\le 4.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
