    "q-132237": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132237",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>8)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>8)=P(X\\ge 9)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\ge 9$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 9) & ≈P(Y\\ge 9-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 8.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-132237-a",
              "type": "math",
