    "q-132234": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132234",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X<17)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X<17)=P(X\\le 16)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\le 16$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 16) & ≈P(Y\\le 16+0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\le 16.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
